# Which UCLA ROMS namelist vocabulary each roms_gpu release reads.
#
# A release reads the namelist groups and keys of the UCLA ROMS release named
# here, plus its own optional groups below. Groups it does not read are
# ignored; a CPU feature switch it does not have stops the run at start-up
# (src/host/feature_guard.F90). From v0.1.2-beta, a key it does not know in a
# group it reads stops the run at start-up, naming the group (before, the rest
# of that group silently kept its defaults).
#
# Keys added in later UCLA ROMS releases that roms_gpu does not read (the run
# stops if they are present):
#   0.12.0  &cdr_lite_settings  cdr_carbonate_sensitivity_time_interpolation
#   0.13.0  &v_sponge_settings  v_sponge_trc
#
# GPU-only additions: the optional group &tile_settings (tile balancing),
# &passive_tracers (n_passive, init_mode, write_passive), and in
# &param_settings the keys n, nsub_x, nsub_e and ntrc_bio.
#
# Surface restoring: UCLA ROMS selects it with cpp keys, which the GPU model
# cannot see; roms_gpu switches it on with GPU-only logical keys in
# &surf_frc_settings (default .false., bulk forcing only), and reads the
# coefficient from the same group as UCLA ROMS:
#   CPU cpp key        roms_gpu &surf_frc_settings   coefficient group (cm/day)
#   SFLX_CORR          sflx_corr = .true.             &sss_correction dSSSdt
#   QCORRECTION        qcorrection = .true.           &sst_correction dSSTdt
#   CFLX_CORR (MARBL)  cflx_corr = .true.             &dic_alk_correction dCdt
# A forcing file holding the restoring data (sss, sst, sDIC/sALK)
# while its switch is off gives a start-up warning. The restoring-flux
# output (&surf_flx_output_settings wrt_rstflx) is not on the GPU.
#
# Pressure fluxes for nesting: &calc_pflx_settings calc_pflx and
# pflx_timescale as UCLA ROMS (the group is optional here; absent means
# off). UCLA ROMS computes up/vp only when built with the DIAGNOSTICS cpp
# key; roms_gpu computes them whenever calc_pflx = .true., with the
# internal-tide pressure of ucla-roms eae883ee, writes up_<side>/vp_<side>
# to the child boundary file for objects whose output_vars name them, and
# keeps u_slow, v_slow, p_slow in the restart. pflx_timescale must be > 0
# when calc_pflx is on (the run stops otherwise).
#
# Sponge tuning for nested children: &sponge_tune_settings ub_tune (the CPU
# needs the SPONGE_TUNE cpp key as well; the GPU only the switch) tunes the
# inflow nudging of the open boundaries to the parent's up/vp of the
# boundary files; it needs calc_pflx = .true. (the run stops otherwise), as
# UCLA ROMS. wrt_sponge writes <output_root_name>_spn.<date>.nc every
# output_period_sponge (nrpf_sponge records per file): the child and parent
# fluxes and the coefficient of every open side, averaged over the period
# (sponge_avg) or of the output step, as UCLA ROMS with its fixes of
# 2026-11 (sponge-tune-pio-fixes). As UCLA ROMS's precheck, with restarts
# and wrt_sponge on, nrpf_sponge * output_period_sponge must be positive
# and divide output_period_rst (the run stops otherwise). The coefficients
# ub_west, ub_east, ub_south, ub_north are restart fields, written after
# the step's tuning (exact restarts), as in that version of UCLA ROMS.
#
# Half-resolution forcing: interp_bulk_frc, interp_flux_frc
# (&surf_frc_settings) and interp_bgc_frc (&bgc_settings) are read but not
# used; roms_gpu takes a forcing field as half resolution from its shape
# ((LLm/2 + 2) x (MMm/2 + 2) at rho points, xi one shorter at u points,
# eta one shorter at v points) and interpolates it as UCLA ROMS does with
# the key on. A field that fits neither the model grid nor these shapes
# stops the run.
#
# Per-tracer lists: &vertical_mixing_settings akt_bak and &tracer_diff2 tnu2
# accept one value per tracer, as in UCLA ROMS (up to 512), in its tracer
# order (T, S, nt_passive generic, CDR_LITE, MARBL). Only akt_bak's T and S
# entries are used (as on the CPU, the other tracers mix with salinity's
# diffusivity). tnu2 is used per tracer, as UCLA ROMS with TS_DIF2: each
# tracer's harmonic diffusivity is its tnu2 plus the v_sponge ramp. Generic
# passives added by the GPU-only &passive_tracers n_passive beyond nt_passive
# take salinity's tnu2.
#
# roms_gpu      UCLA ROMS namelist
